From 4b37836f85c3ba3af9a7b20f67e3915b3fa3d509 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcelo Alcantara <maralc@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:36:47 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "iommu/apple-dart: Support T8140 DARTs and
 firmware-owned stream roots"

This reverts commit 79379798f12fdb32ba79f74b0524cfc4f0170471.

It breaks the display DARTs of t600x: on a MacBook Pro 14" M1 Pro
(j314s) 28930c000, 28c304000, 28c30c000 and 38b30c000 fail with
"failed to publish host page-table entries: -5" and probe error -16,
so no DCP binds (simpledrm at 60 Hz, no external display) and the
CD321x controllers, which wait on DCP's Type-C routes, never probe.
apple_dart_hw_sync_locked() now fails on TTBR indexes that have no
locked root, which the old code skipped, and apple_dart_publish_root()
refuses slots the firmware already fills, which DCP relies on Linux
taking over. Omarchy carries this revert until the T8140 handling is
limited to the DARTs that need it.

Tested 2026-09-30 on the M1 Pro: with this revert all DARTs and DCPs
bind, eDP runs at 120 Hz and the external display returns.
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 714 ++++++-------------------------------
 1 file changed, 112 insertions(+), 602 deletions(-)

